::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-spec, dependencies: list(tomet-ast, tomet-config, tomet-formatter, tomet-parser, tomet-printer, tomet-spec-derive, tomet-tree), dependents: list(tomet-cli)}

=[tomet-spec]

==[tomet-spec]

Automated `.tmt` specification and reference generation for CLI commands (`clap`)
and configuration schemas (`#[derive(Config)]`).

==[Architecture & Responsibilities]

- ("Single-Crate Consumer Surface") Re-exports [`Config`] (`#[derive(Config)]`), [`ConfigSpecProvider`],
[`ConfigGroupSpec`], and [`ConfigEntrySpec`] so external repositories
can define configuration schemas and render `.tmt` specifications by
depending only on `tomet-spec`.
- ("Pure In-Memory AST & `.tmt` Generators")
  - ([`cli`]) Converts `clap::Command` introspection trees into `.tmt` [`Document`](tomet_ast::Document) ASTs and formatted strings.
  - ([`config`]) Converts [`ConfigGroupSpec`] slices into `.tmt` [`Document`](tomet_ast::Document) ASTs and formatted strings.
  - ([`util`]) Shared inline code escaping and AST construction utilities.

==[Module cli]

CLI command reference generator from `clap::Command` definitions.

===[Functions]

====[fn render]

Renders a complete formatted CLI specification `.tmt` string from a `clap::Command`.

====[fn document]

Builds a Tomet [`Document`] AST representing the CLI command hierarchy and options.

====[fn push_command]

Appends sections, usage, arguments, options, and subcommands for `cmd` into `out`.

==[Module config]

Configuration reference generator from [`ConfigGroupSpec`] schemas.

===[Functions]

====[fn render]

Renders a complete formatted configuration specification `.tmt` string from [`ConfigGroupSpec`] slices.

====[fn document]

Builds a Tomet [`Document`] AST representing the configuration groups and entries.

====[fn push_group]

Appends a level-2 section and entry list for `group` into `out`.

====[fn entry_item]

Builds a list item element describing a single [`ConfigEntrySpec`].

==[Module util]

Shared AST helpers and formatting utilities for specification generators.

===[Functions]

====[fn dummy]

Returns a dummy source span for synthesized AST nodes.

====[fn text]

Builds a plain text inline node.

====[fn code]

Builds an inline `@raw` code span node.

====[fn paragraph]

Wraps inline nodes into a paragraph block.

====[fn code_block]

Builds a block-level `@raw(lang: "text")` code block element.

====[fn list]

Builds an unordered list from an iterator of list item elements.

====[fn inlines]

Parses text with `` `code` `` spans turned into inline `@raw` code spans,
and escapes element-like trigger words (`@`, `$`, `^`).

====[fn guard_triggers]

Splits plain text so every element-looking word (`@foo`, `$bar`, `^baz`) is wrapped in a code span.

====[fn paragraphs]

Splits prose on blank lines (`\n\n`) and normalizes internal whitespace per paragraph.
